# Case study

## Writing SQL queries
*bindings, design pattern, new syntax,
 etc*

- C# T-LINQ
- F# first-class query expression .cite {fs-query}
- OCaml caqti, petrol, sequoia, quel .cite {quel}, irmin
- Elixir ecto

## QueL .cite {quel}
*Suzuki Kenichi (knih), Oleg Kiselyov
 (okmij), .br Yukiyoshi Kameyama
 (Programming Logic Group)*

```reason
let q = observe @@ () =>
	foreach(products) @@ o =>
	yield (o)
```

.speakernote
	`observer @@ () =>` does look like the decorator pattern

<<<

```reason "SQL query as a functor"
module _ (S : SYM_SCHEMA) = {
	open S;
	let products = table("products", products());
	let q = observe @@ () =>
		foreach(products) @@ o =>
		yield o
}
```

```reason "\"Concretize\" query into string"
let module M = Ex(GenSQL);
print_endline(M.q)
```

